  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` for the fireworks harbor. `typecheck` passes, but I couldn't run or build the app, so I haven't seen a frame and the look is untested. Brightness values (spark emissive, bloom, burst glow, point-light intensities) are guesses and may need tuning once someone views it.\n\n- **Sky:** a large inverted sphere with a custom shader. It draws a dark gradient, a faint horizon haze, about 650 twinkling stars, and a soft glow around each active burst.\n- **Water:** a custom-shader plane with a calm, stretched ripple pattern. It reflects the sky and each active burst as shimmering vertical streaks.\n- **Shoreline:** a dark shore box, hills, rocks, 13 small buildings with roofs and a few warm windows, a pier with posts and a lamp, and 7 boats.\n- **Sparks:** each of six colors (gold, red, blue, green, violet, silver) has one instanced-sphere node for the bright phase and one for the dimmer phase. A spark switches to the dim node partway through its life, then shrinks to nothing. Six pooled sparks nodes exist per color, so there are 12 instanced nodes in total.\n- **Rockets:** they launch from the shore at irregular intervals, with an occasional quick follow-up. Each rises with a short glowing trail and then explodes.\n- **Bursts:** there are four types: single shell, double shell with a contrasting core, a streaked shell, and a gold willow. All have drag and gravity, and sparks live roughly 1.7 to 3 seconds. The streaked types shed short trails.\n- **Lighting and camera:** three point lights move to the newest bursts and tint the buildings. Bloom is on. The camera is fixed, with no drift.\n- **Contract:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame with `bursts` and `activeParticles`. `activeParticles` includes trail particles. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`.\n\nI couldn't confirm that the engine recomputes culling bounds when `setInstances` changes the instance count. As a precaution, each spark node keeps two tiny hidden anchor instances that span t",
